  "claim_boundary": "This record supports retaining the lifecycle-derived 0.7.0/v3 ordinary request reset policy on the exact installed BUILD_TESTING=OFF mainline artifact. At P1024, P4096, and P8192, all six matched B/C pairs reduce the external-TTFT-minus-pure-Prefill bridge and all 24 warmup plus measured requests preserve complete generated text, SSE termination, usage, finish, and route receipts. Pure Prefill and Decode move only at mixed or noise-scale directions, so this record does not claim a material TTFT, Prefill-throughput, or Decode improvement. The same-server P40000 lifecycle proves that committed-prefix reset costs 15.185065 ms versus 17.504564 ms for conservative full reset, while three successful P40000 requests preserve identical server witnesses and raw output/SSE/usage/finish/route receipts. The P40000 bundle does not retain the complete external content-event arrival timeline, so its derived external TTFT and Decode figures have no evidence authority; its single-sample long-Prefill differences are not attributed to reset. This is ordinary-default retention evidence, not complete accuracy, capability, repetition, target-SLO, release, or production qualification.",
